==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|praetermitto|lang=la}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|pretermits|pretermitting|pretermitted}}

# To intentionally [[disregard]] something, allow it to go [[unnoticed]], or change the subject in response to someone's comment; to [[omit]] or fail to carry out something; to prematurely [[terminate]] or [[interrupt]] something.

Example: For seeing there is no Common-wealth in the world, wherein there be Rules enough set down, for the regulating of all the actions, and words of men, (as being a thing impossible:) it followeth necessarily, that in all kinds of actions, by the laws praetermitted, men have the Liberty, of doing what their own reasons shall suggest, for the most profitable to themselves. (Hobbes, Leviathan)

#: {{rfquotek|Francis Bacon}}

